    {
      "dom_id": "question-69983",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "The vector $a$ is directed horizontally to the left and has magnitude \n $8$, while the vector $b$ is directed vertically up and has magnitude $6.$ Which of the following is a unit vector that is parallel to $a+b?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we have to find $a+b.$ According to the triangle law of addition, the resultant $a+b$ goes from the tail of $a$ to the head of $b:$   \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14253719/assets/19a22ffd49677b2ff17b4c69908280dcfcf30695c63ae4bb6e4ab83441146194.png)\n\nTo find the unit vector corresponding to $a+b,$ we have to divide by the magnitude: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTo find the magnitude, first notice that we obtain a right triangle. So, we can use the Pythagorean theorem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{|a+b|}^{2} & ={|a|}^{2}+{|b|}^{2} \\\\  & ={8}^{2}+{6}^{2} \\\\  & =64+36 \\\\  & =100\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the magnitude is\n\n$$\n|a+b|=\\sqrt{100}=10\n$$\n\nand the corresponding unit vector is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}(a+b).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
